1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:07,632
现在，这绝对不是一本我期望你们中有人看过的书
Now, this is definitely not a book I would expect any of you to have ever come across, okay?

2
00:00:07,632 --> 00:00:09,419
Amy Morin，她的故事非常感人
Amy Morin, incredibly touching story.

3
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:14,761
我在领英上找到她，发消息给她，她是一位了不起的生活教练
I found her on LinkedIn, messaged her, and she’s an incredible life coach.

4
00:00:14,761 --> 00:00:18,979
我最欣赏她的故事的一点是，这故事很个人
What I really like about her story is it’s personal, okay?

5
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:20,989
我认为，任何拥有个人故事的人
I think anyone that’s got a personal story

6
00:00:20,989 --> 00:00:22,775
那些经历过切身触动的——那些切身经历——
that’s been personally touched—that personal experience—

7
00:00:22,775 --> 00:00:24,116
是你可以从中学习的东西
is something you can learn from.

8
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:30,648
而那些没有切身经历的人，或没有真实生活经验的人
that don’t have skin in the game, or that don’t have real-life experiences.

9
00:00:30,648 --> 00:00:32,280
而Amy Morin绝对有这些经历
And Amy Morin definitely has it.

10
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,760
如果你读了这本书的简介，你就会理解为什么
If you read the synopsis of the book, you’ll understand why.

11
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:38,280
她经历过一些真正的悲剧，并且克服了它们
She’s had some real tough tragedies to overcome.

12
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:44,942
但在理解她经历的这些悲剧时，她不得不克服很多心理弱点
But in understanding those tragedies she’s had, she’s had to overcome a lot of mental weaknesses.

13
00:00:44,942 --> 00:00:48,719
而这些心理弱点是我们每个人都有的
And it’s those mental weaknesses that we all have, okay?

15
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:50,584
我们中没有人能对Amy的经历无动于衷
None of us are indifferent to Amy.

16
00:00:50,584 --> 00:00:54,868
我们都有这些弱点，我们都会在生命中的不同时刻遇到这些弱点
We all have these weaknesses. We all come across these weaknesses at various times in our lives.

17
00:00:54,868 --> 00:00:57,640
这正是这本书特别值得一读的原因
And this is why this book is particularly good to read.

18
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:04,260
需要注意的是，她是一名博主，所以显然你也可以在YouTube上看她的视频
Note, obviously, she’s a blogger, so you can obviously watch some YouTube videos of her as well.

20
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:10,308
从总结来看，这是为了避免我们都容易犯的心理陷阱
In terms of summary, it’s to avoid the mental pitfalls that all of us are prone to, okay?

21
00:01:10,308 --> 00:01:11,899
所以她突出了这些陷阱
So she highlights those pitfalls.

23
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:15,139
这几乎就像是说，她要列出十大事项——
It’s almost like saying, you know, she’s going to put down the top ten things—

24
00:01:15,139 --> 00:01:17,383
你可能会犯的错误
you’re likely to make the mistakes you’re going to make,

25
00:01:17,383 --> 00:01:20,936
结果会是什么，以及你如何克服它们
and what the outcomes are going to be, and how you’re going to have to overcome them, okay?

28
00:01:27,409 --> 00:01:31,936
这样你就能识别出自己正走向那个陷阱，并同样避免陷进去
you can identify yourself heading into that pitfall and avoid getting into it equally.

30
00:01:31,980 --> 00:01:37,820
如果你真的陷入其中一个弱点，你也能很快走出来
If you do fall into one of those weaknesses, You can very quickly get yourself back out.

32
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:42,880
显然，一些关键亮点包括：自省以及对相似性的认知
In terms of, obviously, some of the key highlights: self-reflection and recognition of similarities.

33
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:52,500
困境的实际案例和实际解决方案，理解大多数人会犯的心理错误及如何避免
Practical examples of hardship and practical solutions. Understanding the mental errors most humans make and how to avoid them.

35
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:55,935
然后理解这些问题发生的根本原因
And then understanding the underlying reasons why they’re occurring.

36
00:01:55,935 --> 00:01:59,988
有时候，我们倾向于看一个问题，只想解决它
Sometimes, we tend to look at a problem and just want to solve it,

37
00:01:59,988 --> 00:02:03,462
但除非你理解问题的根本原因
but you can never really find an effective solution unless you understand

38
00:02:03,462 --> 00:02:06,937
否则你永远找不到一个有效的解决方案
what the underlying cause of the problem was in the first place.

41
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:10,464
在把潜意识坏习惯
In terms of transforming unconscious bad habits

42
00:02:10,464 --> 00:02:14,699
